<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - May rating raised to buy.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - May rating raised to buy.</headline>
<text>
<p>--Rodman &amp; Renshaw Inc said Friday it upgraded its rating on May Department Stores Inc to buy from neutral, citing the retailer's commitment to top-line growth and a record of expense control that will allow it to benefit in an improving apparel environment.</p>
<p>--Rodman also raised its EPS estimates to $2.86 from $2.83 for FY97 and to $3.30 from $3.22 for FY98.</p>
<p>--It noted that May's year-to-date comparable-store sales of 4.9 percent are the best in the department store industry.</p>
<p>--May was trading at 47-5/8, up 3/8.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
